title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

The KPD has few allies but many enemies. Even just making the other parties ambivalent towards us may make our growth easier. How the SPD may react to us reaching out to them may be interesting...

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the left-liberal German Democratic Party and conservative-liberal German People's Party.
- @center: Strengthen our bonds with the Catholic Center Party.
- @spd: Work towards repairing relationships with the social democrats.
- @kpd_alone: The KPD can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@spd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; spd_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: kpd_blutmai if blutmai = 1; spd_1 if blutmai = 0 and spd_coalition_success = 0 and (spd_relation < 40 or kpd_rectified_history = 1); kpd_rectification_of_history if spd_relation >= 40 and kpd_rectified_history = 0; spd_2 if spd_coalition_success = 1 and kpd_rectified_history = 1

@spd_1
on-arrival: spd_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if spd_inter_party_seen <= 1; marxist_leninist_dissent += 2; left_opposition_dissent += 2

The social democrats and our own party are suspicious of this move, especially the SPD reformists , who persist in calling us "red fascists". However, connections are made at the grassroots and local levels.

@kpd_rectification_of_history

One stumbling block for our relations with the SPD is our history of conflict, dating back to 1918 and 1919. The we is especially contemptuous of Gustav Noske, the SPD "bloodhound" who reportedly ordered the violent suppression of the Spartacist uprising and other KPD revolts. They're also to blame  for the deaths of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht, two SPD-turned-KPD leaders who were killed during the suppression of the uprising.

For further improvements in KPD relations, it is  necessary for the SPD to expel Noske, and hold some sort of commemoration for Luxemburg and Liebknecht.

- @yes_history: Yes, they've must apologize for our past actions.
- @no_history: No, they have no need to apologize.

@yes_history
choose-if: spd_relation < 50
unavailable-subtitle: Hah, as if their leadership actually likes us that much.
on-arrival: marxist_leninist_dissent -= 6; reformist_strength -= 2; left_opposition_dissent += 5; conciliator_dissent -= 6; conciliator_strength += 5; kpd_rectified_history = 1; spd_relation += 8*(1-dissent)

As part of normalizing relations with the us, the SPD have to acknowledge the wrongdoings of the past. They have expelled Noske, and have held public commemorations for those killed by troops during the uprisings.

This was a suprise to everyone in the party and has made even the more hardline "social fascist" beleivers more accepting of temporary cooperation.

@no_history
choose-if: spd_relation <= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Wait, they're actually going to apologize?!.
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 5

The SPD refuses to apologize for the actions of Ebert and Noske; claiming is the our fault for launching a violent insurrection.


@spd_2
on-arrival: spd_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if spd_inter_party_seen <= 1; conciliator_dissent -= 2;

After the success of the coalition government with the SPD, they are much more amenable to us.

@kpd_blutmai
on-arrival: spd_relation += 3*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 1

After the events of Blütmai, reconciling with the social democrats is near imposible. Still, their leftist faction make relations possible.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; z_relation += 2 if z_party_leader == "Joos"
go-to: center_op if z_in_government = 1 and spd_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Brüning"; center_coalition if kpd_in_government = 1 and z_in_government = 1; center_bruning if chancellor = "Brüning"

@center_op
on-arrival: z_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)

Why did we do this? Of course they're still not going to like us.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: z_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

Though normally opposed, we have decided to mutually quiet our discontent for eachother to maintain the popular front.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: z_relation += 0*(1 - dissent)

What, why? You think Brüning is suddenly going to like us now?

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ddp_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)
go-to:  dvp_loss if year <= 1930; dvp_moribund if year > 1930

The [+ ddp_name +]'s only use is for passing progressive social legislation.

@dvp_loss
on-arrival: dvp_relation += 0*(1 - dissent)

Little does the rest of the party know, this action is actually a front for funneling party money into Wittorf's pockets...



@dvp_moribund
on-arrival: dvp_relation += 0*(1 - dissent)

You, player, should be purged from the party. why are you trying to be allies with a dying liberal party ruled by industrialists?


@kpd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
